WinHTTP response decompression and server certificate chain backport.

Based on Wine upstream commits by Hans Leidekker and Michael Green:
20b34866f318617c854818dc59fa7b8e8b87c0c6 (stream prerequisite),
335ae4237c72f09408e9b1b26b1d5f3891ed9a3c (decompression),
a1a13c25374dd5e80b5837fe574cfa967ac53efb (certificate chain),
93ef2498b391902e560f0e4aa64a7c74abe40b4a (handle state),
f27d14a21cfef776cbd5c7871a269066e3f1dc87 (retain verified TLS chain).
Adapted to the pinned Wine/HTTP2 transport. Decode only opted-in encodings,
keep query/read byte counts decoded, and reject invalid/truncated gzip data.
Wine LGPL-2.1-or-later notices remain in the corresponding source files.

